    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nUpdates normative tagging and rule metadata to align with the “impl-def” model and the latest docs-resources schema support.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Renames the normative tag `ENDIANNESS_LITTLE_OR_BIG` to `ENDIANNESS` across AsciiDoc, exported norm-tags JSON, and rule definitions.\n- Updates RV32 normative rule definition for endianness to use `kind: base` with `instance: Any` and mark it as implementation-defined behavior.\n- Removes `impl-def-behavior: true` from the `FLEN` rule in the F extension and bumps the `docs-resources` submodule.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 5 out of 5 changed files in this pull request and generated 2 comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/rv32.adoc | Renames the inline normative anchor ID for the endianness rule. |\r\n| ref/riscv-unprivileged-norm-tags.json | Renames the exported norm-tag key and updates references in the chapter tag list. |\r\n| normative_rule_defs/rv32.yaml | Renames the endianness rule and adds base/Any schema fields + impl-def marker. |\r\n| normative_rule_defs/f-st-ext.yaml | Removes impl-def marker from FLEN. |\r\n| docs-resources | Updates submodule commit to a version supporting `base: Any`. |\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
